		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4652&amp;p=34731#p34731"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div><blockquote class="uncited"><div>When new features are added to the firmware, the text in the firmware and CPS is only in English.<br><br>We rely on volunteers to translate to other languages and often new features do not get translated</div></blockquote>This is not a new function. It was already available in older CPS. <br>It is translated in the translation file. Therefore the field should be translated.<br><br>Regards René</div></blockquote>OK.<br><br>That means that there is a linkage problem in the translation file, i.e the UI control name does not match the name in the translation file or the translation item is not in the correct place in the heirarchy, because the translations are applied automatically if the linkage is correct<br><br><br>Edit.<br><br>It looks like this is a 'case' sensitivity problem<br><br>dmo  vs DMO<br><br>I'll need to update either the UI or the xml files so that the name is an exact match including the upper case 'DMO'<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Tue Dec 17, 2024 8:31 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
